      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced dynamic recovery causes lower elevated-temperature strain hardening in FeNiCrMn than in CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperatures, Co-free FeNiCrMn will show a more rapid decline in flow stress than the baseline alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation density and local short-range ordering vary with temperature and strain rate and mediate the mechanical response.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A crossover between low-temperature dislocation drag and high-temperature dynamic recovery should be observable.",
